<section data-view id="community" class="chapter editorial community-index">
<nav class="trail" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="#top" data-i18n="directoryHome">Home</a></nav><h1 data-i18n="ed_community">Test together, from build to release.</h1><p class="chapter-lead" data-i18n="ed_communityLead">Find another developer who will try your app on their phone. Give their project the same attention and keep working together as your builds change.</p>
<div class="track-list"><a class="track-link" href="#community/mutual"><span class="track-state" data-i18n="edMutState">Before release</span><div><h2 data-i18n="edMutTitle">Mutual testing</h2><p data-i18n="edMutBody">Run a closed test with peers. See what a day of testing involves before you join.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true" class="track-chevron">›</span></a><a class="track-link" href="#community/growth"><span class="track-state" data-i18n="edGrowState">After release</span><div><h2 data-i18n="edGrowTitle">Published apps</h2><p data-i18n="edGrowBody">Bring a live app and a question about the next release. See how people actually use it.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true" class="track-chevron">›</span></a></div><nav class="editorial-related"><a class="route-link" href="#community/mission" data-i18n="edMissionLink">Mission & principles</a><a class="route-link" href="#trust" data-i18n="edTrustLink">Community in numbers</a><a class="route-link" href="#build" data-i18n="edBuildLink">Open roles & ideas</a></nav>
</section>
<section data-view id="community/mutual" class="chapter editorial ">
<nav class="trail" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="#top" data-i18n="directoryHome">Home</a> <i aria-hidden="true">/</i> <a href="#community" data-i18n="navCommunity">Community</a></nav><h1 data-i18n="ed_mutual">Run a mutual closed test.</h1><p class="chapter-lead" data-i18n="ed_mutualLead">You test a partner’s app and they test yours. Choose a workload you can keep up for at least 14 days. Each project has its own start and finish.</p>
<div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edPrepH">Before the first check-in</h2><div><p data-i18n="edPrepP">List your build in the Mini App and check that the testing link opens. Agree on one task a new user should be able to finish. Put your current phone model in your profile.</p></div></div><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edDailyH">On a testing day</h2><div><p data-i18n="edDailyP">Try the task on your phone and check in. Send checkpoint screenshots through the platform to the Chat Hub on time. Daily reports have room for comments, bugs, ideas and Google Play test feedback.</p><p data-i18n="edTeamTime">About 30 minutes of hands-on use across the whole team each day is a useful planning target. Share the time across real tasks.</p></div></div><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edFinishH">When your own test finishes</h2><div><p data-i18n="edFinishP">Your app can move to review while a partner still has days left. Finish each exchange you accepted. Leaving early affects Reliability. Complaints or suspicious activity may lead to an account block or project removal.</p></div></div><div class="editorial-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="#community/rules" data-i18n="edReadCode">Read the participant code</a><a class="route-link" href="https://t.me/googleplay_console_12testers/31/8296" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="edFullGuide">Full platform guide in Telegram</a></div>
</section>
<section data-view id="community/growth" class="chapter editorial ">
<nav class="trail" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="#top" data-i18n="directoryHome">Home</a> <i aria-hidden="true">/</i> <a href="#community" data-i18n="navCommunity">Community</a></nav><h1 data-i18n="ed_growth">Published apps</h1><p class="chapter-lead" data-i18n="ed_growthLead">Store discovery depends in part on app quality and sustained interest. A live release lets you watch where people get stuck, ship a fix and invite them back to the same task.</p>
<div class="live-track notranslate" translate="no">Google Play · Live</div><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edSelfH">Work directly with developers</h2><div><p data-i18n="edSelfP">Add your published app to the Mini App. Give someone a task, such as restoring a purchase on a new phone. Ask about clarity, ease of use and stability. Bugs and suggestions give you a reason to follow up after the next release.</p><a class="route-link" href="#community/rules" data-i18n="edJoinLive">Read the code and join</a></div></div><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edCoordH">Hand coordination to the team</h2><div><p data-i18n="edCoordP">A coordinator manages reciprocal tests and keeps the team moving. Follow activity in the bot and compare changes in your own Play Console. Start the conversation with the link to your app and the question you want answered.</p><a class="route-link" href="#services/growth" data-i18n="edCoordLink">Explore managed growth</a></div></div>
</section>
<section data-view id="community/mission" class="chapter editorial ">
<nav class="trail" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="#top" data-i18n="directoryHome">Home</a> <i aria-hidden="true">/</i> <a href="#community" data-i18n="navCommunity">Community</a></nav><h1 data-i18n="ed_mission">Why we test each other’s work</h1><p class="chapter-lead" data-i18n="ed_missionLead">DevTestHub brings independent developers and digital creators together. Google Play is our focus today. A developer who met your app in closed testing can still help you shape its tenth release.</p>
<div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edRecipH">Keep the exchange fair</h2><div><p data-i18n="edRecipP">Take the same care with a partner’s build that you hope for with yours. Finish the tests you accepted, even when your own app is already up for review.</p></div></div><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edSpecificH">Give the author something to try</h2><div><p data-i18n="edSpecificP">“Back closed the editor and lost my draft on this phone” gives an author a place to look. Share the steps, then try them again when the fix is ready.</p></div></div><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edTrustPrincipleH">Make trust visible</h2><div><p data-i18n="edTrustPrincipleP">A profile keeps a record of work across projects. Reliability, Karma and Contribution help a new partner understand how you work before they commit two weeks.</p></div></div><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edChoiceH">Leave room for an honest verdict</h2><div><p data-i18n="edChoiceP">We study how stores surface useful apps and work ethically. A public rating, a purchase and the choice to keep an app all belong to the person using it.</p></div></div><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edInitiativeH">Let participants shape the platform</h2><div><p data-i18n="edInitiativeP">If three newcomers stumble on the same step, bring that observation to the team. You can propose an experiment, try it with a small group and own the change.</p></div></div><div class="editorial-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="#community/rules" data-i18n="edReadCode">Read the participant code</a><a class="route-link" href="#build" data-i18n="edBuildLink">Open roles & ideas</a></div>
</section>
<section data-view id="community/rules" class="chapter editorial ">
<nav class="trail" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="#top" data-i18n="directoryHome">Home</a> <i aria-hidden="true">/</i> <a href="#community" data-i18n="navCommunity">Community</a></nav><h1 data-i18n="ed_rules">The participant code</h1><p class="chapter-lead" data-i18n="ed_rulesLead">These five agreements apply when you take on a project. Read them before you open the Mini App and choose your first partner.</p>
<ol class="code-list"><li><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="ed14H">Plan for 14+ days</h2><div><p data-i18n="ed14P">Stay opted in throughout the agreed cycle. Check each project’s schedule in the Mini App before taking on more work.</p><details class="code-extension"><summary data-i18n="edReserveTitle">If the project needs more time</summary><p data-i18n="edReserve">The owner can extend the cycle and reserve a $BUST reward for the team’s additional testing days.</p></details></div></div></li><li><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edDutyH">Finish every exchange</h2><div><p data-i18n="edDutyP">Keep testing your partners’ builds after your own one moves to review. Leaving early affects Reliability. Complaints and suspicious activity can lead to a suspension or project removal.</p></div></div></li><li><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edRealH">Test a real task on your phone</h2><div><p data-i18n="edRealP">Keep your device model up to date in your profile. Walk through a real task and send checkpoint screenshots to the Chat Hub through the platform. Aim for about 30 minutes of meaningful activity per day across the team.</p></div></div></li><li><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edHonestH">Keep feedback independent</h2><div><p data-i18n="edHonestP">Record what you actually saw. We do not support inflated activity or fake ratings. You decide whether to leave a public review. Partners cannot require a five-star rating in return for testing.</p></div></div></li><li><div class="field-note"><h2 data-i18n="edCapitalH">Build a record others can trust</h2><div><p data-i18n="edCapitalP">Reliability reflects how you keep commitments. Karma records recognition, and Contribution tracks confirmed work. Your $BUST balance is separate and can fund platform rewards.</p></div></div></li></ol><div class="ack" id="community-gate"><label class="ack-check"><input type="checkbox" id="community-ack"><span data-i18n="edAck">I have read the code and will finish the exchanges I accept.</span></label><p class="ack-wait" id="community-wait" data-i18n="edWait">Confirm to open the bot and Mini App.</p><div id="community-actions" class="entry-actions" hidden><a class="button button-outline" href="https://t.me/Android12TestersBot?start=web_mutual" data-bot-link="bot" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="edBot">Open the Telegram bot</a><a class="button button-primary" href="https://t.me/Android12TestersBot/app" data-bot-link="app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="edApp">Enter the Mini App</a><p class="entry-hint" data-i18n="edBotHelp">The bot sends updates to your chat. Open the Mini App to list your project and choose partners.</p></div></div>
</section>
<section data-view id="build" class="chapter editorial ">
<nav class="trail" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="#top" data-i18n="directoryHome">Home</a></nav><h1 data-i18n="ed_build">Build DevTestHub with us.</h1><p class="chapter-lead" data-i18n="ed_buildLead">Pick a piece of the platform you would like to own. One issue you have seen first-hand and a small change you can try are enough to start.</p>
<h2 class="subsection-title" data-i18n="edOpenRoles">Open roles</h2><details class="topic"><summary data-i18n="edArchitectH">Community architect</summary><p data-i18n="edArchitectP">Design an exchange that gets two developers talking about a real problem. Run it with a small group and see whether the author gets a useful answer.</p></details><details class="topic"><summary data-i18n="edQAH">Bug hunting, QA & localization</summary><p data-i18n="edQAP">Try a complete flow in the bot or Mini App. Bring the build, device, steps and the phrase that made you expect a different result.</p></details><details class="topic"><summary data-i18n="edSMMH">SMM & communications</summary><p data-i18n="edSMMP">Turn an actual test into a story another developer would save. Show the original issue, the fix and what changed on the tester’s phone.</p></details><details class="topic"><summary data-i18n="edMentorH">Newcomer mentor</summary><p data-i18n="edMentorP">Stay with someone through their first exchange. Note where they need help and bring recurring questions back to the product team.</p></details><h2 class="subsection-title" data-i18n="edInWork">In development</h2><details class="topic"><summary data-i18n="edMarketH">DevTestHub app market</summary><p data-i18n="edMarketP">A catalogue where people can discover independent apps by the job they need done. Help design the very first search.</p></details><details class="topic"><summary data-i18n="edIdeasH">Open ideas hub</summary><p data-i18n="edIdeasP">A place to propose an improvement, discuss it with other members and vote on what the community should try next.</p></details><details class="topic"><summary data-i18n="edNetworkH">Developer advertising network</summary><p data-i18n="edNetworkP">A way for vetted indie apps to introduce each other to interested audiences inside and beyond the community. Help define relevance and consent.</p></details><p class="contact-note"><span data-i18n="edFounder">Have a direction in mind? Tell the founder what you would try first.</span> <a href="https://t.me/garantXchange" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@garantXchange</a></p>
</section>
<section data-view id="faq" class="chapter editorial ">
<nav class="trail" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="#top" data-i18n="directoryHome">Home</a></nav><h1 data-i18n="ed_faq">Questions before you start</h1><p class="chapter-lead" data-i18n="ed_faqLead">Choose the question closest to the decision you are making.</p>
<div class="faq-list"><details><summary data-i18n="seoFaq1q">Who needs 12 testers for 14 days?</summary><p data-i18n="seoFaq1a">For personal Google Play developer accounts created after November 13, 2023, at least 12 testers must stay opted in continuously for the 14 days before you apply. Once that condition is met, you can request production access in Play Console. Google reviews the application.</p><a class="route-link" href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/14151465" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="googleRequirementsLink">Google Play testing requirements</a></details>
<details><summary data-i18n="seoFaq2q">How does mutual testing differ from private testing?</summary><p data-i18n="seoFaq2a">In a free exchange, developers use each other’s builds and check in daily. With private testing, DevTestHub coordinates 12 or more testers on real Android devices. You follow the work without taking on partner apps.</p></details>
<details><summary data-i18n="seoFaq3q">Why plan for 14+ days?</summary><p data-i18n="seoFaq3a">The minimum opt-in period is continuous. We usually schedule a full 15 days for a managed test, allowing a buffer for time-zone boundaries and Play Console updates. In an exchange, keep each partner’s agreed end date.</p></details>
<details><summary data-i18n="seoFaq4q">What does the $75 review add to the basic test?</summary><p data-i18n="seoFaq4a">The basic test covers team activity and help answering the production-access questionnaire. It costs $20 with crypto or $23 with PayPal or bank transfer. The $75 total includes a written app review with device coverage, reproducible issues and a prioritized fix plan. Arrange it with the team in Telegram.</p></details>
<details><summary data-i18n="seoFaq5q">How do I connect testers to my build?</summary><p data-i18n="seoFaq5a">Add <code>google-play-dev-test@googlegroups.com</code> to the tester groups for your closed track. Make the build available in the required regions, send the changes for review and share the Android testing link. You keep sole control of your Play Console.</p></details>
<details><summary data-i18n="seoFaq6q">Can the team test a paid app?</summary><p data-i18n="seoFaq6a">Add the tester group in Play Console’s License testing settings as well as in the closed track. Keep the license response at <code>RESPOND_NORMALLY</code>. The setup guide shows both places.</p></details>
<details><summary data-i18n="seoFaq7q">What if Google asks for more testing?</summary><p data-i18n="seoFaq7a">Send us the review response. We continue testing until you receive production access or refund the service fee. You handle any code or policy changes Google requests. Google makes the final access decision.</p></details>
<details><summary data-i18n="seoFaq8q">Why does the bot use Telegram Stars?</summary><p data-i18n="seoFaq8a">Telegram requires Stars for digital services sold inside bots and Mini Apps. Choose Stars there, or use crypto, PayPal or bank transfer on this website. You can attach a receipt and follow the order in your account.</p></details>
<details><summary data-i18n="seoFaq9q">Can I join with an app that is already published?</summary><p data-i18n="seoFaq9a">Yes. List the app in the Mini App and choose a task for other developers to try. They can assess clarity, ease of use and stability, document a bug or suggest a change. Public store reviews are always voluntary.</p></details>
<details><summary data-i18n="seoFaq10q">What does a growth coordinator take on?</summary><p data-i18n="seoFaq10a">The coordinator organizes the team, manages reciprocal tests and follows up on participation. You set the product question, watch activity in the bot and compare the outcome with your Play Console data. Discuss scope and terms before handing over coordination.</p></details></div>
</section>
